{{also|Muffin}}
==English==

===Etymology===
The origin is {{unk.|en|title=unknown}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmʌfɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-muffin.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌfɪn|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|British|lang=en}} a type of [[flattish]] bun, usually cut in two [[horizontally]], [[toast]]ed and spread with butter, etc, before being eaten
# {{context|US|lang=en}} A type of individual bread such as corn, bran, banana or zucchini bread often sliced and spread with butter, etc before being eaten.
# {{context|especially US|lang=en}} (informally) A cupcake without frosting, but sometimes glazed.
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} a [[mechanism]] used in the [[w:Java Network Launching Protocol|Java Network Launching Protocol]] [[analogous]] to the [[cookie]] mechanism and which permits a program running in a [[browser]] to perform operations on a client machine
# {{context|slang|lang=en}} a term of endearment<!--, e.g. "nuffin' muffin"-->
# {{context|sexual slang|lang=en}} a [[vulva]]
# {{context|baseball|slang|lang=en}} a less [[talented]] player; one who [[muff]]s, or drops the ball
# {{context|slang|lang=en}} a charming, attractive young man

====Quotations====
'''computing term'''
* '''2001''': The name/value pairs provided by the PersistenceService are similar to browser cookies. The Java Web Start implementation honors this legacy by naming the pairs "'''muffins'''." &mdash; ''JNLP and Java Web Start'', Sun Developer Network, Technical Articles and Tips, 30 May 2001.
'''the vulva'''
* '''1989''': I wanna be stuffin’ Martha’s '''muffin'''!!!, &mdash; Mojo Nixon and Skid Roper ''Stuffin’ Martha’s Muffin''.

====Synonyms====
* (''flattish bun''): [[English muffin]] (''US'')

